WEBVTT

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.690
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.500
The future, probably Japan.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.500
Robots have long been in practical use,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.450
and practical use of androids has just begun.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.600
Question, again.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:23.840
Yes, master.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.300
When did you last go out?

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.000
Two days ago.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.000
The reason?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.200
Shopping for groceries and clothing items.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.400
An order from Mother -

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.600
You did something beyond your orders?

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.400
I have not.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.550
It doesn't make sense . . .

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.000
These days you're treating it like a person.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.000
That's what mother does!

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.690
What's she got to do with it?

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.400
The other day, dressing it up like a doll.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.300
Our parents' generation is hopeless.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.800
It would be totally android-holic if you did that!

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.100
Breakfast.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.160
Understood.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:56.800
You mean the so-called houseroids, right?

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.150
They basically have no emotions or individuality.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.500
And yet android-holic youth empathize with them.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.300
They're that bad at communicating with real humans.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.800
See what I'm saying?!

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:12.900
Status, Sammy!

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.800
Housecleaning this morning.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.560
This afternoon I am scheduled to go shopping.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:26.850
<i>There it is.</i>

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:27.780
<i>I recognize it.</i>

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.000
<i>Finally, it's here!</i>

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.200
<i>Master, I brought your change of clothes.</i>

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.300
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.500
<i>You say thank you?</i>

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.700
<i>You don't?</i>

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.700
<i>No way!</i>

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:36.660
<i>You're android-holic!</i>

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:37.790
<i>What's that?!</i>

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.800
Says it didn't go to that cafe.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.500
But what about that thing, on your mobile . . .

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.000
The movement log?

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:44.900
That's it.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.000
Maybe I made a mistake.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.200
That's what I'm saying - you trust robots too much!

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.600
You're saying Sammy is lying?!

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.840
Aha!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.300
I mean . . . the android at home.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.620
So you call it Sammy!

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.000
It's not like I trust it.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.760
Recite the Three Laws of Robotics.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.000
Hey, this isn't law school!

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.500
Master, get your act together. Recite them.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.400
The first law is . . .

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.700
Do no harm to humans.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:08.400
Right!

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.400
The second law.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.000
Obey orders given by humans,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.700
as long as they don't contradict the first law.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:13.500
Not bad!

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.710
The third law . . .

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.380
You're sure there is one?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.310
Protect yourself.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.300
That's the basis of robot behavior . . .

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.400
That's what it's all about!

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.200
About what?

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.350
I'm saying this:

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.700
There is no law saying don't tell lies.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.760
You're kidding!

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.500
It's surprising how people don't know this.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.610
Anyway, it means you can't trust Sammy.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.000
Says it's going shopping this afternoon!

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:37.800
What!?

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.150
I'm talking about Sammy!

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.520
Says it's only going shopping!

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.300
Only one way to know if that's true.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.300
We've got to go and see for ourselves.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.370
You really going in?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.770
What, you don't want to find out?

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.500
That's not it . . .

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.200
So let's go.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:55.800
. . . sure.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:56.410
What's that!?

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.170
I said I'm going!

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.000
Then let's go!

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:58.500
Let's go!

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.000
Time of Eve's house rule:

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.100
No discrimination between humans and robots.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.120
Welcome!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.000
What's the matter?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.260
It's too early to know for sure . . .

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.670
It might show up later.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.300
Time of Eve

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.300
You want to wait here?!

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.200
For now, let's stick around until dinner.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.800
But I really don't want to run into it . . .

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.300
This is a good spot.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.320
I'm really nearsighted.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.960
You can't even see from here?

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.580
I can hardly see without my glasses . . .

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.890
Chie, come on down from there -

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.940
I'm a cat!

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.940
Apologies, young men.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.600
Children need their freedom . . .

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.200
. . . right?

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.200
She sure is free.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.300
Hey, I told you to stop it!

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.300
Those round things are strange!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.000
Chie, there's something you want to eat, right?

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.100
I'm a cat!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.370
Ice cream!

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.000
You've got to sit down if you want to eat!

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.100
Ice cream! Ice cream!

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.300
Apologies.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Something gets her attention,

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.500
and she forgets everything else.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.000
It's a piano.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.000
You going to play?

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.500
I told you, I've quit . . .

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.300
. . . playing, that is.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.900
That guy and the child are humans, right?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.180
They sure look like humans . . . but . . .

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.700
What?

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.260
Akiko also seemed human when she was here.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
I'm lonely.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.100
Hey, I'm lonely.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.300
We can't see each other everyday?

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.200
But . . . I've got work too.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.000
You're seeing another girl outside, aren't you?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.300
It's not like that!

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.100
Don't leave me on my own.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.280
Yes, I know.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.300
Shall we sit somewhere else?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.200
What have you been doing?

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.500
Socializing.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.600
Place your order!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.600
Two Blends.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.800
Two Eve's Blends!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.000
Ice cream!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.500
Chie, sorry to make you wait!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.000
My delicate cat tongue can handle cold things!

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.600
You're scared, aren't you?

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.590
Chie, you're so clever with words!

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Of what?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.300
Sammy showing up.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.400
What are you talking about!

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.600
Your own robot, coming to an unknown place,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.900
doing things on its own.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.700
An encroachment on human dignity!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.900
Is that your old man talking?

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.000
But I wouldn't know. I don't have a robot.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.800
And I wonder why that is . . .

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.000
I'm here!

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.400
I just don't get why Sammy would lie.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.000
I don't get robots without rings.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.040
I'll be right back.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.950
It's Rikuo!

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.530
Hey, what's the matter?

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.990
Stop looking at me like that!

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.250
You're completely different . . .

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.540
Really!? I'm so pleased!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.320
Um . . . that's not what I meant!

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.390
Question!

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.500
What happened to the ring? Above your head?

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:30.600
It's turned off.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.700
If I don't look like a human, I'll break the rule.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:33.800
But robotic law!

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:34.850
OK! Enough of this talk!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.000
I'm a cat!

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.500
Chie, what are you doing?

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:46.700
There's something strange on his face.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.040
You want something with me? Is this Blade Runner?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.890
How about you do a better job at surveillance?

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:20.030
Having a guy's eyes glued to me -

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.200
it isn't pleasant.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.300
I'm sorry.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.900
Break the rule, and you won't have a good time here.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.300
Or rather, there's no point in being here at all.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.380
Or so I hear.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.000
I don't have it!

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.200
Goodbye. Give my regards to your friend.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.570
You can get them back later. Probably.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:50.900
Probably?

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.680
Before she hid my hat -

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.140
My glasses were stolen!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.200
Your hat?

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.130
My hat?

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:56.950
You said she hid it.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.900
Right! I asked where she hid it -

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.600
and she had it all along!

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:02.800
Meaning?

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.090
She had it in her panties!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:06.900
Seems she liked my hat a lot.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.480
Something I have to take care of just came up.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.280
Seems you're enjoying yourselves.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.680
What's the matter with Masaki?

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:22.880
You can't open it right now.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.000
It locks for a while after someone leaves.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:26.960
What are you talking about?!

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.460
Privacy is important.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.200
Is this size OK?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.810
We have something bigger too.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.200
The people at home will find it if it's too big.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.880
OK, OK. Wait a sec.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.440
I'll give you a good selection.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.000
Rina, what should we do?

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.770
Excuse us. Let us go first.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.270
Here's today's order.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:07.600
Sorry for the trouble.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:08.800
It's the cafe's coffee and everything.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:09.900
Do they like it?

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.000
I wonder . . .

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.200
You can always ask them yourself.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.300
That's impossible.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.500
Why?

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.720
They don't like it when I do things on my own.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:22.120
They tell me not to do anything on my own.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.490
I'm sure they'll understand.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.000
The cafe's rule is local!

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.200
No comparison with robotic law!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.300
Another rule violation! I'm telling!

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.400
There's no way to talk about this?!

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:31.760
I'll keep it a secret from Nagi.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:32.880
Let's drop the subject!

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.790
Secret?

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.200
So, you can keep a secret?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.900
You two are having quite a strange conversation.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.740
Everyone has one or two secrets.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:45.550
But she's -

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.350
No discrimination between humans and robots.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:52.240
I have some things I'm keeping secret from Chie.

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.410
It's not like I don't lie.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.820
But it's for her benefit.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.360
The things Akiko is keeping secret . . .

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.740
. . .are for you, Rikuo. Right?

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.000
Don't bring harm to humans.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.100
That's the basis for robot behavior.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.200
You did something beyond your orders?

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.300
I have not.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.260
Because I'll be harmed.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.320
It's for me.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.870
After all, she didn't tell you where your glasses are

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:22.000
because she wanted you to play with her.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.300
Aren't they in her panties?

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.550
Said she gave them to someone.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
It's so late!

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.100
You're going?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.200
I've got to get dinner ready.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.600
Thanks for this.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:38.970
You finally noticed!

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.100
Why didn't you tell me?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.200
You didn't ask.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:44.120
The customers and staff are so chummy?

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:26.360
Rikuo

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:27.860
What's going on!?

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.000
Rikuo.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.940
It's acting on its own!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.550
That's my -

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:33.860
Sit down!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.650
OK . . .

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.200
I'll treat you to a cup on the house.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.100
That girl . . .

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.300
When did she come here the first time?

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.100
At first she was at a loss,

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.140
but gradually she opened up.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.500
She opens up?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.140
She talks about a lot of different things.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.670
The mother who buys her clothes.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.500
Occasional nightmares.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.530
The boy who's stopped playing the piano.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
And the other day she said to me -

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.120
she wants to make a good cup of coffee.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Seems she worries a lot.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.000
Worries?

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:27.390
She's not sure . . .

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.110
. . . if the things she's doing are right . . .

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.830
. . . or wrong . . .

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:35.020
Here you go.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.300
If you just follow the rule,

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:44.800
you're always welcome at Time of Eve.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.050
And then I lost him there.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.000
You followed him outside?

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.580
I wanted to see if that guy had a ring above his head.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.500
There's definitely something up with that cafe -

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:15.920
I'm thinking of going back again.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.510
I'll go with you!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:19.600
I'll get to the bottom of this mystery!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.830
See you later. Say hello to robot Sammy for me.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.000
Question.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:35.440
What is it?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.240
. . . that cafe . . .

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.490
Master, I am sorry -

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:43.900
Coffee.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.340
Understood.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.280
The coffee these days . . .

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.600
. . . it's good . . . maybe.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.360
Thank you.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.490
You can see lots of different interesting things . . .

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.480
Nothing specific yet, but . . .

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.150
No relation with the Ethics Committee?

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.900
They wouldn't use such a lousy shadow.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:12.000
I'll let it go on for a while, and see what happens.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:13.910
Yes . . .

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:20.400
Dr. Ashimori, individualism is starting to take root . . .

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.090
and that means that the restraint circuit -

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.230
Assumptions will just lead you away from the truth.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.870
That's what Shiotsuki would say.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.990
I'll continue . . .
